["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/standardName", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The name of a relevant standard that may apply to an artifact.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N36fd05042b414037a7f77f60217b42ab", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#nodeKind", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#Literal", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/SsvcDecisionType/track", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The vulnerability does not require action at this time. The organization would continue to track the vulnerability and reassess it if new information becomes available. CISA recommends remediating Track vulnerabilities within standard update timelines.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/EvidenceType/observation", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Documentation of direct monitoring or witnessing of the demonstration of processes, tests, or any kind of system responses during a specified timeframe under specified environmental conditions.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RequirementStatusType", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Provide an enumerated set of requirement statuses that can provide state to a requirement.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N8bf6efa4bdc446259f3ab384b85f5684", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest", "_:Nad1274bdf58f4d5eb27b45f2a3018dee", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isil", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Identifier for Libraries and Related Organizations (ISIL)](https://slks.dk/english/work-areas/libraries-and-literature/library-standards/isil/) is a unique alphanumeric code for identifying libraries, archives, museums, and related organizations standardized by [ISO 15511](https://www.iso.org/standard/77849.html). It consists of a prefix\u2014which may be an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code or a non-country code assigned by the ISIL Registration Authority\u2014followed by a unit identifier, totaling up to 16 characters (e.g., `FI-Sipoo-S\u00f6` or `ZDB-1-SBD`). Valid symbols include any alphanumeric character, solidus (`/`), hyphen-minus (`-`), or colon.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/evaluation", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty", "globalId", "", ""]
